<BaseLayout title="Jackson County Personal Injury Lawyers | Michigan Accident Attorneys" description="Experienced Jackson County personal injury attorneys with 45 years handling tough Michigan cases. Free consultation. No fee unless we win. Call (734) 994-0200.">
  <ArticleContent>
    <h2><strong>Experienced Personal Injury Lawyers Serving Jackson County, Michigan</strong></h2>
    <p>When you're injured in an accident in Jackson County, you need attorneys who understand Michigan's complex legal landscape and have a long record in the courtroom. At Logeman &amp; Iafrate, P.C., we've spent more than 45 years fighting for injured people throughout Jackson County—from the City of Jackson to Blackman Township, Summit Township, and all surrounding communities.</p>
    <p>We take cases other firms turn down and prepare every case for trial. Insurance companies throughout Michigan know our reputation, and they know we prepare every case for trial. Our record reflects decades of verdicts and settlements, from catastrophic injury cases to securing no-fault benefits that insurers tried to deny.</p>

    <h2><strong>Personal Injury Cases We Handle in Jackson County</strong></h2>
    <p>Our Jackson County personal injury practice covers the full range of accident and injury claims:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Car accidents:</strong> Michigan's no-fault system is complex and confusing. We help Jackson County accident victims navigate PIP benefits and pursue third-party claims when injuries meet the serious impairment threshold.</li>
      <li><strong>Truck accidents:</strong> Commercial vehicle collisions on I-94, US-127, and other Jackson County roadways often result in catastrophic injuries requiring experienced legal representation.</li>
      <li><strong>Motorcycle accidents:</strong> Riders face devastating injuries when struck by negligent drivers. We fight to hold at-fault parties accountable and secure full compensation.</li>
      <li><strong>Construction accidents:</strong> Jackson County's construction sites pose serious hazards. We pursue both workers' compensation and third-party claims for injured workers.</li>
      <li><strong>Premises liability:</strong> Property owners must maintain safe conditions. When they fail and someone gets hurt, we hold them accountable.</li>
      <li><strong>Wrongful death:</strong> Losing a loved one to someone else's negligence is devastating. We provide compassionate representation to Jackson County families seeking justice.</li>
      <li><strong>Catastrophic injuries:</strong> Traumatic brain injuries, spinal cord damage, amputations, and severe burns require comprehensive legal advocacy to secure lifetime care costs.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2><strong>Understanding Michigan's No-Fault Insurance System</strong></h2>
    <p>Michigan's no-fault auto insurance law directly affects every Jackson County accident victim. After a crash, you typically file with your own insurer for Personal Injury Protection (PIP) benefits covering medical expenses, wage loss, and replacement services—regardless of who caused the accident.</p>
    <p>The 2019-2020 reforms changed everything. Depending on your coverage level, your PIP medical benefits may be capped at $50,000, $250,000, $500,000, or remain unlimited. Understanding what coverage you have is critical to your recovery.</p>
    <p>You can sue the at-fault driver only if your injuries meet Michigan's serious impairment of body function threshold—an objectively manifested impairment of an important body function that affects your general ability to lead your normal life. Our attorneys have extensive experience proving threshold injuries and pursuing full third-party recoveries for Jackson County clients.</p>

    <h2><strong>Fighting Insurance Companies That Deny Legitimate Claims</strong></h2>
    <p>Insurance companies routinely deny or undervalue legitimate claims. They argue injuries are pre-existing, treatment is unnecessary, or coverage doesn't apply. We've heard every excuse, and we've beaten them in courtrooms throughout Jackson County and across Michigan.</p>
    <p>Over the decades, we have taken insurers to trial when they refused to honor their obligations. When State Farm, Allstate, Progressive, or any other carrier denies benefits you're entitled to, we're prepared to take them to trial. That trial-ready approach is what separates us from high-volume settlement mills and gets our clients the compensation they deserve.</p>

    <h2><strong>What Compensation Can You Recover?</strong></h2>
    <p>Depending on your case type, Jackson County accident victims may recover:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>No-fault PIP benefits for medical expenses, lost wages, and attendant care</li>
      <li>Pain and suffering compensation in third-party claims</li>
      <li>Excess economic damages beyond PIP limits</li>
      <li>Loss of consortium for family members</li>
      <li>Compensation for permanent scarring and disfigurement</li>
      <li>Future medical care and lifetime attendant care costs</li>
      <li>Lost earning capacity for permanently disabling injuries</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Every case is different. Our attorneys evaluate your specific situation, explain your options clearly, and work to recover the full compensation you're owed.</p>

    <h2><strong>Why Jackson County Residents Choose Logeman & Iafrate</strong></h2>
    <p>Jackson County families trust us because:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>We have more than 45 years of trial experience</strong> handling tough personal injury cases throughout Michigan</li>
      <li><strong>We take cases other firms refuse</strong></li>
      <li><strong>We prepare every case for trial</strong>—insurance companies know we are ready</li>
      <li><strong>Free consultations and contingency-fee basis</strong>—no fees unless we win</li>
      <li><strong>Deep expertise in Michigan's no-fault system</strong> and complex insurance battles</li>
      <li><strong>Decades of verdicts and settlements</strong> in serious injury cases</li>
      <li><strong>Compassionate support</strong> during the most challenging times of our clients' lives</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don't just handle cases—we fight for justice. Whether you're dealing with mounting medical bills after a Jackson County car crash, facing an insurance company that's denying no-fault benefits, or coping with permanent disabilities from a workplace accident, we're here to help you rebuild your life.</p>

    <h2><strong>Schedule Your Free Consultation with Jackson County Personal Injury Attorneys</strong></h2>
    <p>If you or a loved one has been injured in an accident in Jackson County, it's worth acting promptly to protect your rights. Michigan's statutes of limitations and insurance filing deadlines can affect your ability to recover compensation.</p>
    <p>At Logeman &amp; Iafrate, P.C., we offer free consultations to evaluate your case and explain your legal options. We operate on a contingency-fee basis—we don't get paid unless we win your case. That means you can afford experienced, trial-ready attorneys from day one.</p>
    <p>Contact our Ann Arbor office today to schedule your free consultation. Call <strong>(734) 994-0200</strong> or fill out our online contact form. Let us fight by your side and help you rebuild your life after an accident.</p>
    <p>We take cases others won't, and we prepare every case for trial. Decades of representing injured clients throughout Jackson County and Michigan.</p>
  </ArticleContent>

